{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#long249:thm:signed-interpolation","Sparse interpolation around the totient","<p>Fix\nintegers <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, and any function <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span>. There exist <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and target-independent sets <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>, with\nevery element of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> even, such that\nevery</p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\">equals <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for an\ninteger sequence <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></math></span>\nsatisfying:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></math></span>. In\nparticular the prefix through <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi></math></span> and\nevery odd coefficient are unchanged.</p></li>\n<li><p>For every fixed <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, both\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> are divisible by <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi></math></span> eventually, with a cutoff independent\nof <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>.</p></li>\n<li><p>For every fixed <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, the\ndefect <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nequals an integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></math></span> for\nall sufficiently large <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>H</mi></math></span>.\nThe cutoff is independent of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>. If\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>P</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>P</mi></math></span>, this defect is zero at every\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>H</mi></math></span>.</p></li>\n<li><p>For each root of unity <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ζ</mi></math></span>, the radial function <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nextends smoothly to <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. Its Taylor\ncoefficients there lie in <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span>. The coefficients of\norders <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>P</mi></math></span> are zero if the order\nof <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ζ</mi></math></span> is at most <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi></math></span>.</p></li>\n<li><p>For every fixed <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> the\nabsolutely convergent series</p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>n</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>c</mi><mspace width=\"0.444em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\">extends to an entire\nfunction, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></math></span>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>The set <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> has upper Banach\ndensity zero. The set <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi></math></span> has\nordinary density zero and upper Banach density one. Define</p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">min</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">inf</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p>For large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, and one constant <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>C</mi></math></span>, independent of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>, gives</p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">min</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p>Thus every block length <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is preserved\nasymptotically.</p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#long249:cor:signed-observations","Observations that do not determine\nirrationality","<p>The following data, taken together, do not determine\nwhether <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is\nrational: the fixed prefix and odd coefficients; every fixed eventual\ncoefficient and cumulative congruence; the block laws on scales <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>; fixed progression moments\nmodulo eventual integer constants outside <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi></math></span>; progression Dirichlet functions modulo\nentire functions; and radial germs at all roots of unity modulo smooth\nfunctions with Taylor coefficients in <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span>. This remains true with\nexact equality of the first <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi></math></span>\nmoment degrees and first <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi></math></span> radial\nTaylor coefficients at moduli and root orders at most <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi></math></span>.</p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#long249:prop:signed-first-harmonic","The first-harmonic test on the rational\nmembers","<p>Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> be integers with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></msup><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>v</mi></math></span> is odd and positive. Choose <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>v</mi><mo>∣</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup></math></span>, then for every\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>,</p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#lem:orbit","The doubling identity","<p><em> For all\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nso <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mspace width=\"0.444em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and consequently the exact first character of the tail\ndifference is the <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> orbit of\none real number: </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Hence, for fixed <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span>, the phases <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> are\nthe forward orbit of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> under <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:transfer","Transfer to the doubling orbit","<p><em> Suppose that </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>89</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>X</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This hypothesis implies that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is irrational.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#cor:digitform","A digit version of the analytic\ncondition","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\ndenote the proportion of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nwith <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>. If for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>\nthere are cofinally many <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi></math></span> with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is irrational. For nondyadic <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></math></span>, the condition counted by <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is exactly a change between\nbinary digits <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>. Thus the same sufficient hypothesis\nasks for at least <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>11</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn></math></span> such\nchanges, counted with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi></math></span>,\non arbitrarily large blocks for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:lacunary","The block norm condition is stronger in\nthe class <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span>","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> if <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></math></span> for some <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> otherwise, so <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> for all <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></msup></math></span>. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>β</mi></math></span> is irrational, and for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>81</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>&gt;</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>X</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Consequently the block norm condition\nfails for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>β</mi></math></span> at every\nsufficiently large scale, for every admissible truncation depth, even\nthough <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>β</mi></math></span> is irrational. Thus\nirrationality, nonnegative integer coefficients and the bound <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> do not imply the block gap. A\nproof for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> needs an additional\nproperty not shared by this example; the comparison does not specify\nwhich additional property will suffice.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:dickman","A one-sided bound for the\nunassigned terms","<p><em> Fix <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></math></span> and\nchoose the admissible depth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi></math></span>\nminimally for each large <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi></math></span>. Put\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mi>X</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>X</mi></msqrt></math></span>. If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></math></span> is unassigned, then its largest\nprime factor satisfies <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></math></span>.\nConsequently </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"bottom top\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>X</mi></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> for all sufficiently large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi></math></span>. Here <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> counts the positive integers at\nmost <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></span> whose prime factors are all\nat most <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></span>. This is an upper bound\nfor the unassigned count, not an asymptotic equality for that\ncount.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:badcof","The excluded-cofactor estimate","<p><em> Fix <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></math></span> and use the minimal\nadmissible depth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi></math></span>, as in\nProposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:dickman\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:dickman\">12.6</a>;\nthus <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. For\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>m</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>,\nwith natural density <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>; by\nSchoenberg’s theorem <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi></math></span> exists, is\ncontinuous, and <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> <span\nclass=\"citation\" data-cites=\"schoenberg1928\"><a href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#ref-21\">[21]</a></span>, in the framework\nof <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"schoenberg1936\"><a href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#ref-22\">[22]</a></span>. Then\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> so a single choice of\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>η</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>200</mn></math></span> meets the <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>X</mi></math></span> bound for all large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi></math></span>. This choice fixes <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>η</mi></math></span> before <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span>, as required. It supplies only the\nexcluded-cofactor bound: the mean and mean-subtracted estimates must\nstill hold for this same <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>η</mi></math></span>, and\ndo not follow from making <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>η</mi></math></span>\nsmaller.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:route4","","<p><em> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> holds whenever <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#res:fulldepth","Propagation of one nonintegral tail\ndifference","<p><em> Fix <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>, then every\nsufficiently late pair <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>\ncontains an <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span> such that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> holds. Consequently </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nRequiring this for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> is equivalent to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#res:rankonefloor","A lower bound for the rank-one\nquotients","<p><em> For <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>, the denominator of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is positive, and the unique\nminimiser is <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Every\nadmissible quotient and every nonempty finite positive weighted average\nof such quotients satisfies </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>320</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The\nuniform bound <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>15</mn></math></span> is\nfalse already at <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>.</em></p>"]],"source":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.json?v=e6abdbcd8877"}
